From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: drop pre-Round-27 HANDLE-style Identifier construction
 in ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp

Update 34 (fixing the round-34 CLANG64/CLANGARM64 ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
1-error block at [8347]/[8293]):

ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp:330 fails with
  error: no matching constructor for initialization of 'IPC::Connection::Identifier'
  didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID, IPC::Connection::Identifier {
    reinterpret_cast<HANDLE>(static_cast<intptr_t>(serverSocketValue)) });
                                                 ^  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
The clang++ candidate list (Connection.h:298/300/301/305/309) shows only
the USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) branch's constructors:
  * Identifier() = default
  * Identifier(Identifier&&) = default
  * explicit Identifier(Handle&&)              -> takes ConnectionHandle
  * explicit Identifier(UnixFileDescriptor&&)  -> takes UnixFileDescriptor
The OS(WINDOWS)-branch constructor `explicit Identifier(HANDLE handle)`
at Connection.h:320 is NOT in the candidate set, which means the
preprocessor picked the USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) branch.

Root cause: Round 27 (commit b9c8176, "unify MinGW GTK IPC to unix-flavored
attachment/semaphore types") changed PlatformUse.h to unconditionally
#define USE_UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS=1 for PLATFORM(GTK)||PLATFORM(WPE) on
Windows, so the MinGW GTK build picks the unix-flavored Identifier
(UnixFileDescriptor payload wrapping a Win32 SOCKET handle) and the
OS(WINDOWS)-branch Identifier(HANDLE) constructor disappears. The
existing ConnectionGLib.cpp was rewritten to the unix flavor in
Round 27 (six call sites in Update 27), and AuxiliaryProcessMain.cpp:110
was migrated in Round 28. The `#if OS(WINDOWS)` block at
ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp:328-336 was a pre-Round-27 leftover that the
flavor migration missed — it still constructs Identifier from a raw
HANDLE, which the unified Identifier class no longer has a constructor
for.

Fix: drop the `#if OS(WINDOWS) ... #else ... #endif` block at
ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp:328-336 and use the unix-flavored code path
on Windows too. The kept code is byte-identical to the original
pre-0003 code (which was the `#else` branch):

    RunLoop::mainSingleton().dispatch([protectedThis = protect(*this),
        this, serverSocket = WTF::move(webkitSocketPair.server)] mutable {
        didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID,
            IPC::Connection::Identifier { WTF::move(serverSocket) });
    });

webkitSocketPair.server is a UnixFileDescriptor (IPCUtilities.h:55-58
defines `struct SocketPair { UnixFileDescriptor client; UnixFileDescriptor
server; }` under `#if USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) || OS(WINDOWS)`), and
Identifier(UnixFileDescriptor&&) is the constructor the kept code
invokes. The Win32 SOCKET handle packed inside the UnixFileDescriptor
is created by `IPC::createPlatformConnection()` (also in
IPCUtilities.h) which on Windows returns a bound UDP loopback socket
pair (the Round 22 / Round 27 winsock datagram IPC path).

The `#include <windows.h>` added by 0003 at the top of the file is
still needed: terminateProcess() further down uses OpenProcess() /
TerminateProcess() / CloseHandle() / HANDLE / DWORD / PROCESS_TERMINATE
under its own `#if OS(WINDOWS)` guard, and that block is correct as-is
(pure Win32 process control, not IPC flavor-dependent).

Sandbox verification: pre-patch source reproduces the
`no matching constructor for initialization of 'IPC::Connection::Identifier'`
error against a synthesized MSYS2 CLANG64 configuration
(USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)=1 + OS(WINDOWS)=1, matching PlatformUse.h
on MinGW GTK). Post-patch source compiles cleanly: the kept code
constructs Identifier(UnixFileDescriptor&&), which is in the active
USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) branch. `patch -Np1 --dry-run` on
pristine+0001-0007 applies with 0 .rej / 0 fuzz.

---
 .../Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp         | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
index cda05b2..a3b5f1c 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
@@ -325,15 +325,9 @@ void ProcessLauncher::launchProcess()
     m_processID = g_ascii_strtoll(processIdStr, nullptr, 0);
     RELEASE_ASSERT(m_processID);
 
-#if OS(WINDOWS)
-    RunLoop::mainSingleton().dispatch([protectedThis = protect(*this), this, serverSocketValue = webkitSocketPair.server.release()] mutable {
-        didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID, IPC::Connection::Identifier { reinterpret_cast<HANDLE>(static_cast<intptr_t>(serverSocketValue)) });
-    });
-#else
     RunLoop::mainSingleton().dispatch([protectedThis = protect(*this), this, serverSocket = WTF::move(webkitSocketPair.server)] mutable {
         didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID, IPC::Connection::Identifier { WTF::move(serverSocket) });
     });
-#endif
 }
 
 void ProcessLauncher::terminateProcess()
